{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137572",
      "title": "Exploring Selectors",
      "lectureOrder": 697,
      "videoOrder": 642,
      "sourceHash": "cdb95f382f882bde7ce803c0743accad8b1c6f524944583f9c73a91d2767a4ab",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 3.64,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.64,
          "end": 6.51,
          "en": "we're almost done with this introduction to NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.51,
          "end": 9.15,
          "en": "I now just also wanna explore selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.15,
          "end": 10.38,
          "en": "and then thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.38,
          "end": 14.46,
          "en": "To really conclude this introduction, I also wanna dive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.46,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "into effects and show you what effects are all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "But let's start with selectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 22.014,
          "en": "What are selectors?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.014,
          "end": 26.16,
          "en": "Well, as you learned before in this application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.16,
          "end": 28.89,
          "en": "you can select data from the store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.89,
          "end": 31.56,
          "en": "like here in the counter output component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.56,
          "end": 33.66,
          "en": "with help of the select method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.66,
          "end": 36.48,
          "en": "And here I'm simply selecting the entire state slice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.48,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "or the entire counter, which in my case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "is simply the counter number then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "And I get back an observable to which I can listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 48.474,
          "en": "In this case here with the async pipe, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.474,
          "end": 52.133,
          "en": "Now that's all straightforward and absolutely fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.133,
          "end": 56.58,
          "en": "but there is an alternative or, to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.58,
          "end": 60.53,
          "en": "an addition, to this way of selecting values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.53,
          "end": 63.21,
          "en": "Because whilst this can be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.21,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "for getting the entire state as it's stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "in the store for a specific slice of the store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 72.869,
          "en": "there also can be scenarios and use cases where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.869,
          "end": 76.65,
          "en": "you maybe wanna transform the data that's stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.65,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "in the store before you output it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 80.826,
          "en": "And that's what I wanna show you now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.826,
          "end": 83.73,
          "en": "For that, in that store folder, I'll add a new file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 86.283,
          "en": "counter selectors.ts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.214,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "And I wanted to find all my extra selectors in that file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 92.805,
          "en": "So what's a selector?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.805,
          "end": 96.81,
          "en": "A selector in its simplest form, is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.81,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "that could be stored in a constant, select count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 100.40299999999999,
          "en": "for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.40299999999999,
          "end": 103.045,
          "en": "And then here I'm storing an arrow function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.045,
          "end": 108.045,
          "en": "This selector function will then get a state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.44200000000001,
          "end": 112.505,
          "en": "which is the overall NgRx store state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.505,
          "end": 116.46000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore the shape of that state is the shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.46000000000001,
          "end": 117.723,
          "en": "of your overall store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 122.7,
          "en": "In this demo application here, that would be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.7,
          "end": 125.88,
          "en": "that has all the keys you defined here when you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.88,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "registered the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 130.399,
          "en": "And under those keys, you will find the different values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.399,
          "end": 134.202,
          "en": "stored for these different state slices, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.202,
          "end": 137.621,
          "en": "So for example, a number for the counter reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.621,
          "end": 141.516,
          "en": "Therefore here the shape is an object, which has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.516,
          "end": 144.84,
          "en": "for example, this counter key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.84,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "And the value will be a number because our counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 149.514,
          "en": "state is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.514,
          "end": 154.32,
          "en": "And if you used different key here, instead of counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.32,
          "end": 157.44,
          "en": "you used count, for example, you would have to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 159.213,
          "en": "use that different key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.35,
          "end": 163.53300000000002,
          "en": "But here, I'll stick to counter and revert this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.14,
          "en": "If you had more keys here, you could add them all as keys",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.14,
          "end": 173.7,
          "en": "to this type here for this state and this selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 176.76,
          "en": "But here I need only care about this counter state slice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.76,
          "end": 179.85,
          "en": "And I only have that counter state slice here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.85,
          "end": 181.81,
          "en": "That's why I'm defining the shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.661,
          "end": 186.11599999999999,
          "en": "of my overall store state like this here in this selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.11599999999999,
          "end": 189.57,
          "en": "And then in this arrow function for this selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.57,
          "end": 192,
          "en": "you simply return the value you wanna select.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "In this case, for example, state counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "so that you get the unchanged counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 198.636,
          "en": "as it's stored in the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.636,
          "end": 201.714,
          "en": "That's how you can define a selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.714,
          "end": 205.679,
          "en": "Now, with such a selector defined, you can then export it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.679,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "so that it can be used in other parts of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 212.91,
          "en": "And you then might wanna use this inside of other services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.91,
          "end": 215.999,
          "en": "or Components where you need data from the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.999,
          "end": 219.018,
          "en": "For example, here in the counter output component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.018,
          "end": 223.098,
          "en": "you could now use select count by importing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.098,
          "end": 226.47,
          "en": "from that counter selector's file and use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 226.47,
          "end": 229.96,
          "en": "as a value for the select method on that store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.96,
          "end": 233.861,
          "en": "So instead of just defining the key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 233.861,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "of the state slice you wanna select here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 241.018,
          "en": "you can also pass a selector function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.018,
          "end": 245.962,
          "en": "And why would you do that instead of just defining the key?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.962,
          "end": 249.96,
          "en": "Well, because especially in more complex applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.96,
          "end": 252.69,
          "en": "you of course might have different Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.69,
          "end": 256.08,
          "en": "or services that need to access the same data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.08,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "from your store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "And having one central place where you then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 263.722,
          "en": "define the selection logic could be a good thing to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.722,
          "end": 267.36,
          "en": "because if you then ever change that key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 267.36,
          "end": 270.639,
          "en": "or you change that state value selection logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.639,
          "end": 273.9,
          "en": "you just have to do it in one place instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.9,
          "end": 276.421,
          "en": "of going to multiple Components or services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.421,
          "end": 280.341,
          "en": "And of course, you can also define multiple selectors here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.341,
          "end": 281.7,
          "en": "We could, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.7,
          "end": 286.075,
          "en": "create a never selector called select double count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 286.075,
          "end": 288.776,
          "en": "which gives us the counter times two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 288.776,
          "end": 293.01800000000003,
          "en": "We could define this selector like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.01800000000003,
          "end": 297.802,
          "en": "but you can also use a never nice feature offered by NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.802,
          "end": 301.92,
          "en": "which allows you to combine multiple selectors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.92,
          "end": 304.938,
          "en": "and which allows you to build new selectors based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.938,
          "end": 307.654,
          "en": "on already existing selectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.654,
          "end": 312.654,
          "en": "You can do this with NgRx's, create selector function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 313.62,
          "end": 316.614,
          "en": "which must be imported from NgRx store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.614,
          "end": 320.79,
          "en": "And this function then accepts a list of arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.79,
          "end": 324.033,
          "en": "where every argument is such a selector function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.02,
          "end": 328.23,
          "en": "So you could pass the existing select count function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.23,
          "end": 331.343,
          "en": "as a first argument, and then you could pass a never",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.343,
          "end": 334.92,
          "en": "state selection function as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 334.92,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "And the input for this second argument function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 341.64,
          "en": "will be the return value of this first function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 341.64,
          "end": 345.65999999999997,
          "en": "So in this case here simply a number, because here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 345.65999999999997,
          "end": 348.09000000000003,
          "en": "we get the selected state as it was selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 348.09000000000003,
          "end": 349.65,
          "en": "by this first argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 349.65,
          "end": 352.959,
          "en": "And here I returned the state counter, which is a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 352.959,
          "end": 357.15,
          "en": "You don't even need to add that type annotation because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 357.15,
          "end": 358.89,
          "en": "TypeScript is indeed able to infer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 358.89,
          "end": 362.43,
          "en": "that the value returned by this function will be a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.43,
          "end": 365.31,
          "en": "And then here you could return state times two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.31,
          "end": 367.2,
          "en": "giving you an even shorter way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 367.2,
          "end": 370.079,
          "en": "of defining this selector function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.079,
          "end": 374.28,
          "en": "And that's how you could build more complex selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 374.28,
          "end": 378.21,
          "en": "functions by layering different selector functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 378.21,
          "end": 379.301,
          "en": "on top of each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 379.301,
          "end": 382.599,
          "en": "And now you could also use this selector function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.599,
          "end": 385.44,
          "en": "in a component that needs that state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.44,
          "end": 387.946,
          "en": "For example, the counter output component again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 387.946,
          "end": 391.302,
          "en": "There we could add a never observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 391.302,
          "end": 395.28,
          "en": "the double count observable, let's say, which still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 395.28,
          "end": 399.09000000000003,
          "en": "will be an observable that ultimately yields a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 399.09000000000003,
          "end": 400.40999999999997,
          "en": "But then here in the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 400.40999999999997,
          "end": 403.487,
          "en": "we can set double count equal to store select",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 403.487,
          "end": 407.183,
          "en": "and set that equal to select double count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 407.183,
          "end": 409.74,
          "en": "which of course also must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 409.74,
          "end": 412.526,
          "en": "from the counter selectors file therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 412.526,
          "end": 416.063,
          "en": "But that's how you can then use selectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 416.063,
          "end": 419.64,
          "en": "And now for this component, we could also go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 419.64,
          "end": 422.905,
          "en": "to the template file and also bring back that double counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 422.905,
          "end": 427.905,
          "en": "by outputting double count with help of the async pipe here.",
